{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Maschke","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple.sn_regular_isSemisimpleModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple.sn_regular_isSemisimpleModule","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MaschkeSnSemisimple.lean#L65-L76","doc":"**Existence, regular-module form.** The regular representation `k[S_n]` is a **semisimple\nmodule** over itself — a direct sum of simple submodules, equivalently every submodule has a\ncomplement. This is the module-level face of input 1: the regular representation does decompose\ninto irreducible blocks (Maschke), the only open question being *which* blocks (input 2,\nOkounkov–Vershik). Because the central `C₂ ∈ k[S_n]` stabilises every `k[S_n]`-submodule, this is\nthe \"C₂-invariant subspaces have C₂-invariant complements\" fact from which the block spectral\ndecomposition `mulLeft C₂ = Σ_λ ω_λ·π_λ` is built. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple.sn_isSemisimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple.sn_isSemisimpleRing","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MaschkeSnSemisimple.lean#L56-L63","doc":"**Existence, ring form.** The symmetric-group algebra `k[S_n]` over a characteristic-zero field\nis a **semisimple ring** (Maschke: `char k = 0 ∤ |S_n|`). This is the ring-level face of input 1 —\nthe structural prerequisite for the Wedderburn block decomposition that `SnWedderburnSpectralData`\nassumes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}